ofbx.h / ofbx.cpp — vendored from nem0/OpenFBX, unmodified.

License: MIT (per upstream nem0/OpenFBX; not embedded as a header
comment in these files, same as they ship from upstream).

What this is: a from-scratch (no Autodesk FBX SDK) parser for both text
and binary FBX, including MZ-deflate-compressed binary geometry blocks
(via miniz, see ../miniz/VERSION). `ofbx::load(const u8* data, int size,
u64 flags)` takes the whole file already in memory and returns an
IScene* the caller walks directly (getMeshCount/getMesh/getGeometry/
getSkin/getAnimationStackCount/...) - no file-callback indirection to
route through SDL_RWops the way cgltf's cgltf_load_buffers needs (see
../cgltf/VERSION): this engine's LoaderFbx reads the whole .fbx into one
buffer itself (same SDL_RWops read-loop LoaderX/LoaderGltf already use)
and hands it straight to ofbx::load().

External texture references (Material -> Texture -> a relative/absolute
filename) are still resolved and opened through this engine's own
Texture::load()/setTexturePath(), which is SDL_RWops-backed - ofbx.cpp
itself never opens a texture file, only records the filename string it
read out of the FBX.

Caller contract LoaderFbx.cpp relies on (established by reading the
akadjoker/Radion project's own FbxImporter.cpp, which uses the same
vendored source, as a working reference for correct usage - not a
license/attribution relationship, ofbx is third-party in both
projects):
 - A Mesh's Geometry exposes ONE VERTEX PER FACE CORNER
   (getVertexCount()/getVertices() line up with getFaceIndices()'s
   count/3, not a deduplicated indexed buffer) - a loader that wants a
   normal shared-vertex mesh has to weld afterwards. See the zenblitz
   memory note [[project-gltf-fbx-extension]] and the akadjoker/Radion
   FbxImporter weld-after-import fix from this same session for why this
   matters (that engine's own bug was skipping the weld and shipping
   meshes with ~3x the vertices their triangle count needed).
 - getFaceIndices() winds the LAST index of each polygon as its bitwise
   NOT (~i, i.e. a negative int after the cast) to mark the polygon
   boundary - unwind with `idx < 0 ? -idx - 1 : idx` before using it,
   the same convention loader_x.cpp-style binary formats use for their
   own polygon-boundary marker.
 - A skinned mesh's Skin holds Clusters, each linking one bone (Object*,
   resolved by matching a bone Object's own id against the skeleton
   this engine already built from the FBX's LIMB_NODE objects) to
   per-vertex index/weight pairs (getIndices()/getWeights(),
   getIndicesCount()) - weights are NOT guaranteed already normalized to
   sum to 1 per vertex and NOT capped to 4 influences; both have to be
   enforced by the loader the way Surface::Vertex's fixed 4-slot
   boneBones/boneWeights arrays require.
 - Node/mesh world transforms are D3D-style row-major 4x4 (Matrix::m[16],
   translation in the last row) - same convention LoaderX's
   readFrameTransform already converts to blitz::Transform for .x, reuse
   that shape rather than re-deriving it.
